.\" The text follows the output of `cetli --help --help-all` (app/application.js: add_main_option, GLib and GApplication options), the README and the spec.
.TH CETLI 1 "" "cetli"
.SH NAME
cetli \- small notes on the GNOME desktop that sync between your computers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cetli
.RB [ \-\-autostart ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cetli
keeps short notes in small windows on the GNOME desktop.
Every note is one plain file in a folder, so the folder can be kept in step between computers with a tool such as Syncthing.
The sync window of cetli (menu: Sync) sets up a Syncthing instance of its own after you press a button; it uses
.BR cetli\-sync (1)
for that.
If two computers change the same note before they meet, cetli keeps both versions.
.PP
The package also holds a GNOME Shell extension that puts the note windows back where they were.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-autostart
Start as at login: open only the notes that were left open.
No new empty note is made, the list of all notes and the first\-start sync window are not shown, and when no note was open the program
ends quietly.
If cetli already runs, this call does nothing.
The package starts cetli this way at login of a GNOME session (see
.BR FILES ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help options.
.TP
.B \-\-help\-all
Show all help options.
.TP
.B \-\-help\-gapplication
Show GApplication options.
.TP
.B \-\-gapplication\-service
Enter GApplication service mode (use from D\-Bus service files).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/cetli/notes
The notes, one file per note (\fI\(ti/.local/share/cetli/notes\fR if XDG_DATA_HOME is not set).
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/cetli/backup
Versions of a note that left the notes folder without another copy are kept here.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/cetli/layout.json
Where the note windows were (\fI\(ti/.local/state/cetli/layout.json\fR if XDG_STATE_HOME is not set). It is not synchronised.
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/io.github.trensoft.cetli.desktop
The start at login (\fBcetli \-\-autostart\fR).
To turn it off for one user, put a file with the same name into
.I \(ti/.config/autostart
that holds
.BR Hidden=true .
.TP
.I /usr/share/gnome-shell/extensions/cetli@trensoft.local/
The GNOME Shell extension.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cetli\-sync (1)
